    "title": "Hwy 71 in Wewahitchka reopens after traffic crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Stephanie Pitts ,\n13 hours ago\nUPDATE : Gulf County Sheriff's Office reported that Highway 71 has been reopened.\nORIGINAL STORY:\nGULF COUNTY, Fla. ( WMBB ) - A traffic crash has shut down both lanes of Highway 71 in Wewahitchka on Wednesday morning.\nAccording to the Gulf County Sheriff's Office , the crash occurred on Hwy 71 and Old Transfer Road.\nThe Florida Highway Patrol has reported injuries.\nFire responders are currently on scene. Drivers are urged to use caution when traveling through the area.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
    "summary": "UPDATE : Gulf County Sheriff's Office reported that Highway 71 has been reopened. GULF COUNTY, Fla. ( WMBB ) - A traffic crash has shut down both lanes of Highway 71 in Wewahitchka on Wednesday morning. According to the Gulf County Sheriff's Office , the crash occurred on Hwy 71 and Old Transfer Road. The Florida Highway Patrol has reported injuries. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
